title: room.enter
---
<<if not $hasLens>>
<<get lens>>
<<set $hasLens to true>>
<<endif>>
<<if $examinedFilings>>
<<cel filings 1>>
<<else>>
<<hide scratches>>
<<endif>>
<<if $openedClock>>
<<hide clock>>
<<cel caseDoor 7>>
<<else>>
<<hide caseDoor>>
<<endif>>
===

title: room.look
---
Thorne's workshop. A lantern burns, and of all the clocks here only the tall one in the corner is going.
===

title: clocks.look
---
<<closeup 240>>
Every dial reads seventeen minutes past three.
Hero: A fresh scratch beneath the minute hand. These clocks were stopped by hand.
<<set $examinedClocks to true>>
===

title: clocks.do
---
Hero: Let us preserve the evidence as we found it.
===

title: filings.look
---
<<if $examinedFilings>>
A trail of brass filings, from the bench to the tall-case clock.
<<else>>
Something glints in the sawdust, too fine to make out from here.
<<endif>>
===

title: filings.do
---
Hero: Best not disturb them. My lens will tell us more.
===

title: filings.lens
---
<<walk hero 196 158>>
<<face hero right>>
<<view hero 204>>
<<loop hero 1>>
<<animate hero once>>
Holmes kneels with his lens. Among the sawdust, brass filings catch the lantern light.
<<cel filings 1>>
<<show scratches>>
Hero: A trail from the bench to the tall-case clock. Something was recently fitted there.
<<normal hero>>
<<set $examinedFilings to true>>
===

title: scratches.look
---
Fresh scratches in the boards, where the case clock has been moved and moved back.
===

title: clocks.lens
---
Hero: The lens confirms it: each hand was turned and held.
===

title: clock.look
---
A tall-case clock of polished walnut, its pendulum swinging. The only clock in the shop still going.
Fresh scratches mark the boards beneath it.
===

title: clock.do
---
<<if $deduced>>
<<walk hero 214 160>>
<<face hero right>>
Hero: The clocks did not stop together. Someone arranged them so.
Hero: And this case is far too light for its size.
<<view hero 204>>
<<loop hero 0>>
<<animate hero once>>
<<stop clock>>
<<cel clock 0>>
<<hide clock>>
<<show caseDoor>>
<<sound 130>>
<<animate caseDoor once>>
<<normal hero>>
<<set $openedClock to true>>
<<wait 0.8>>
A stair behind the clock. The air from below is cold.
Hero: Come, Watson. Our clockmaker has left us a way in.
<<elseif $examinedClocks and $examinedFilings>>
Hero: Not yet. Watson, a moment. Let me put this in order aloud.
<<else>>
Hero: Before moving anything, I should examine the wall clocks and the filings on the floor.
<<endif>>
===

title: caseDoor.look
---
Behind the case, a narrow stair descends into darkness.
===

title: caseDoor.do
---
<<walk hero 262 166>>
<<room 103>>
===

title: stair.look
---
<<if $openedClock>>
Behind the case, a narrow stair descends into darkness.
<<else>>
The tall-case clock stands close against the wall.
<<endif>>
===

title: stair.do
---
<<if $openedClock>>
<<walk hero 262 166>>
<<room 103>>
<<else>>
Hero: Before moving anything, I should examine the wall clocks and the filings on the floor.
<<endif>>
===

title: lantern.look
---
The lantern is still warm. Thorne cannot have been gone long.
===

title: lantern.do
---
Hero: Leave it burning. We shall need the light.
===

title: window.look
---
The sash is latched. Rain runs down the glass, and the Clerkenwell roofs dissolve into the dark.
===

title: window.do
---
Hero: Secure from within. No one left by this window.
===

title: bench.look
---
A dismantled movement, a scribbled order and tools laid down in haste.
===

title: ledger.look
---
The last entry is unfinished. A deposit received for an unusual alteration to a clock case.
===

title: watson.look
---
Watson, keeping well clear of the evidence.
===

title: watson.talk
---
-> What do you make of it? <<if not $examinedClocks or not $examinedFilings>>
    Watson: A locked room and a missing man. I make nothing of it yet. You?
    Hero: Nothing, until I have looked properly.
-> The clocks were stopped by hand. <<if $examinedClocks>>
    Hero: Every hand was turned to the same minute and held there. Look at the scratches.
    Watson: But why would a man stop his own clocks?
-> The filings lead to the case clock. <<if $examinedFilings>>
    Hero: Brass, freshly cut, from the bench to that tall-case clock. Something was fitted there, and recently.
    Watson: A repair, perhaps?
    Hero: In the middle of the night, with the door bolted? No.
-> The case clock is a door. <<if $examinedClocks and $examinedFilings and not $deduced>>
    Hero: Every clock here was stopped at the minute he went. All but that one.
    Hero: Its pendulum swings, yet its hands stand at seventeen past three, as still as the rest.
    Hero: It isn't keeping time, Watson. The filings lead to it. That case is a door.
    Watson: Then Thorne didn't vanish at all. He walked through it.
    <<set $deduced to true>>
===

